@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# DroidDeck Mali-first port
+
+This fork is intentionally **Mali-first**. Adreno/Turnip remains as the upstream compatibility
+path, but new GPU abstraction work should be designed around making ARM Mali usable rather than
+adding more KGSL assumptions.
+
+## Stage 1 — backend separation (implemented)
+
+The Android host and the Linux guest are now treated as separate GPU problems.
+
+### Android host compositor
+
+- `DeviceSupport` detects `MALI`, `ADRENO`, `XCLIPSE`, `POWERVR`, or `UNKNOWN`.
+- Adreno continues to load the selected Turnip driver through AdrenoTools.
+- Mali selects Android's **system Vulkan** loader instead of trying an A7xx/A8xx Turnip build.
+- The Wayland compositor asks the Vulkan loader for its supported API version instead of requiring
+  Vulkan 1.3 unconditionally.
+- dma-buf/external-memory/modifier extensions are probed before device creation. They are optional
+  for host startup; missing extensions disable the Vulkan dma-buf import path instead of making
+  `vkCreateDevice` fail.
+- An AHardwareBuffer received through `banner_ahb_v1` counts as valid surface content even when the
+  host Vulkan driver cannot import the companion dma-buf. This keeps the existing SurfaceControl
+  direct-layer path usable on Mali.
+
+### Linux guest
+
+- The runtime no longer silently chooses a Freedreno ICD on Mali.
+- The imported-driver manager accepts generic AArch64 **glibc** Vulkan ICD packages named
+  `libvulkan_*.so`, not only `libvulkan_freedreno*.so`.
+- PanVK/Panfrost/Mali names are preferred for Mali-oriented packages; Turnip/Freedreno remains
+  supported for Adreno.
+- Helper `.so` libraries in an imported ICD package are retained and its directory is exposed in
+  `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` for that session.
+- Android/bionic Vulkan HALs are rejected by the Linux ICD importer; the glibc guest cannot load
+  them directly.
+- `TU_DEBUG` is only applied to the Turnip/Freedreno path.
+- Session diagnostics expose `BL_GPU_FAMILY` and `BL_HOST_VULKAN` and refuse to auto-scan a
+  mismatched Freedreno manifest on Mali.
+
+## The remaining hard problem
+
+There are two materially different Mali kernel situations and they need different guest backends.
+
+### 1. Panfrost/Panthor DRM available
+
+Mesa PanVK can be a real guest Vulkan backend when the device exposes an accessible Linux DRM
+render node backed by Panfrost or Panthor. In this case the next work is to build/package a glibc
+AArch64 PanVK ICD for the DroidDeck rootfs and adapt the Wayland/AHardwareBuffer WSI path.
+
+### 2. Stock Android proprietary Mali (`/dev/mali0` / kbase)
+
+A stock Android Mali Vulkan HAL is normally a **bionic** userspace driver speaking ARM's proprietary
+kernel interface. A normal glibc PanVK build does not magically become compatible with that ABI.
+Copying `vulkan.mali.so` into the rootfs is therefore not a solution.
+
+The Mali-first target for those phones is a bridge rather than pretending `/dev/mali0` is a DRM
+node. The bridge needs to let the glibc guest submit Vulkan work through a host-side Android Vulkan
+implementation and preserve zero-copy presentation through the already existing AHardwareBuffer /
+`banner_ahb_v1` / SurfaceControl path.
+
+Candidate implementation directions to evaluate in Stage 2 are:
+
+1. a Vulkan command/handle bridge between a guest ICD and an Android host service;
+2. a Venus/virtio-style userspace transport if it can be integrated without requiring a privileged
+   kernel virtio-gpu device;
+3. a narrowly scoped bionic-driver compatibility bridge only if it can safely translate the libc,
+   loader, synchronization, gralloc/AHardwareBuffer, and fd semantics needed by the vendor HAL.
+
+The preferred solution is the one that works on **unrooted stock Mali phones** and does not depend
+on vendor-specific private ioctls from one SoC generation.
+
+## Do not regress these invariants
+
+- Never select Turnip merely because Android is new enough.
+- Never fabricate a KGSL render node on Mali.
+- Never let a known Mali device auto-load a Freedreno ICD.
+- Do not require host Vulkan dma-buf modifier import for the compositor to start.
+- Keep AHardwareBuffer direct-layer presentation functional even when Vulkan dma-buf import is
+  unavailable.
+- Treat a Linux guest ICD and an Android Vulkan HAL as different binary/runtime environments.
+
+## Validation status
+
+The source has been statically reviewed and the modified shell session script passes `bash -n`.
+A full Android/NDK Gradle build was attempted, but this working environment does not contain the
+Gradle 8.10.2 distribution and cannot download it. The current build-validation gap is therefore
+an environment limitation, not a reported compiler result.
